note: design 100 (R100.1-2): two calls of the user in a new order: each call pairs with the call of its own callee (the same callee first, then the order), so the step gives new arrows, not two changed call targets
rule+: R100.1-2
must_match: graph: \+3 arrows, −3 arrows
must_not_match: changed call target
=== both Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "depot"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
=== old src/lib.rs
pub fn log(n: u32) -> u32 { n + 1 }
pub fn count(n: u32) -> u32 { n * 2 }

pub fn run(v: u32) -> u32 {
    let a = log(v);
    let b = count(v);
    a + b
}
=== new src/lib.rs
pub fn log(n: u32) -> u32 { n + 1 }
pub fn count(n: u32) -> u32 { n * 2 }

pub fn run(v: u32) -> u32 {
    let b = count(v);
    let a = log(v);
    a + b
}
